# Large data directories — skip traversal entirely (1.6 TB total)
# Trailing * catches version-suffixed sibling dirs too (e.g. crispresso_v2/,
# gatk_v2/) - the REF_VERSION migration (see codes/genome_versions.sh)
# creates these as siblings for some stages, not nested subdirectories, so
# an exact directory name here would silently miss them.
raw_fastq/
trimmed_fastp/
trimmed_trimmomatic/
reference*/
gatk*/
crispresso*/
mapping*/
multiqc_report/
6KAD5R5/
/assembly*/
intermediate_files/

# gatk*/ above is meant for the heavy top-level gatk{,_v2}/ variant-calling
# dirs, but as an unanchored glob it also matches codes/analysis/gatk_summary{,_v2}/
# - small report CSVs/PNGs that should be tracked like their v1 sibling
# already is. Un-ignore explicitly (found 2026-09-15 when gatk_summary_v2/
# came back untracked-but-ignored after parameterizing the GATK report
# scripts for v2).
!codes/analysis/gatk_summary/
!codes/analysis/gatk_summary_v2/

# GenomicsDB workspace — thousands of TileDB binary segment files
gatk/trimmomatic/genomicsdb/
gatk/fastp/genomicsdb/

# Assembly pipeline intermediate/log/downloaded data (scripts in codes/assembly/ stay tracked)
codes/assembly/intermediate_files/
codes/assembly/logs/
codes/assembly/busco_downloads/
codes/assembly/*.log.info
codes/assembly/done_step*_tag
# tgsgapcloser_genome.sh's idempotency tag files, and nextpolish_gapfilled_
# genome.sh's own NextPolish pidNNNN.log.info, both actually land in
# whatever directory the SLURM job was SUBMITTED from (the project root,
# in every run so far - `sbatch codes/assembly/...sh` from off-target_data/),
# not in codes/assembly/ itself - the patterns above never matched them.
# Found 2026-09-17/18 when v2 runs left these sitting untracked at the
# repo root.
/done_step*_tag
/pid*.log.info

# CRISPOR Singularity container + registered genomes - large downloaded/derived
# binaries, regenerable via crispor_add_genomes.sh / crispor_add_genome_v2.sh
# (scripts themselves stay tracked). A 2.4GB .sif + three .2bit genomes ended
# up committed here once (2026-09) and blew up .git to 64GB, causing
# `git push` to die with "pack-objects died of signal 9" (OOM on login node).
codes/analysis/crispor_singularity/*.sif
codes/analysis/crispor_singularity/genomes/
*.sif
*.2bit

# IGV files — track BED features but not large binary GFF3/indices.
# Wildcard (igv_files*) rather than an exact name, same reasoning as
# crispresso*/ above — catches igv_files_v2/ as a sibling too, not just
# igv_files/. Found 2026-09-20 when igv_files_v2/colombian_pseudogenome.gff3.gz
# came back untracked-but-not-actually-ignored (the old exact-name pattern
# never matched it).
igv_files*/*.gz
igv_files*/*.tbi
igv_files*/*.bam
igv_files*/*.bai
igv_files*/*.fna
igv_files*/*.fai

# Test BAMs that ended up in codes/
codes/CRISPResso/test_200.sorted.bam
codes/CRISPResso/test_200.sorted.bam.bai

# fastqc_array.sh's own generated file list - was accidentally committed with
# the author's absolute paths baked in; fastqc_array.sh only regenerates it
# `if [ ! -f "$FILE_LIST" ]`, so tracking it meant a fresh clone would find
# it already present and skip regeneration, silently trying to FastQC files
# at paths that don't exist on a different account. Found 2026-09-22.
codes/filtering/fastqc_trimmed_filelist.txt

# Large data files — catch any stragglers not covered by directory rules
*.bam
*.bai
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf
*.tbi
*.fastq.gz
*.fastq
*.fq.gz
*.fna
*.fa
*.fai
*.dict
*.amb
*.ann
*.bwt
*.pac
*.sa
*.zip
*.tdb
*.tar.gz
*.tar

# SLURM logs
logs/
*.out
*.err

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Temporary files
tmp/
*.tmp
